! PROGRESSIVE INDEXING WITH X0 FETCHES NOTHING -- prepareExec's
! (prog && i1 == 0) clause, VflInt and Connective.
!
! THE RULE.  Reference Manual printed p.21 (PDF 24): "In progressive
! indexing, the value field, bits 0-24 of the index specified by I, is
! used as the effective address.  If progressive indexing with index
! register X0 is specified, indicator OP (operation code invalid) is
! set."  printed p.45 item 15 (PDF 48): "An instruction with invalid
! operation code is executed as NO OPERATION."  decks/
! vfl_progressive_index0.strap pins the refusal's RESULT; this deck pins
! that the refused level asks for no operand.
!
! WHY X0 = 8.0.  vfl_progressive_index0 reports the same clocks with the
! clause deleted (StretchIBox's note, re-measured here: 240 = 240 on a
! plain layout).  The lever is rl_prepare's wait: a level FETCHING word
! 7-15 (eboxRegister) waits for the newest earlier level.  X0's value
! field is the would-be operand address, so pointing it at word 8, the
! accumulator, makes a pointless fetch wait behind the preceding L.
!
! CHECKS: OP on after the first case (OP is set-only, so once), the
! accumulator still PAT after each, X0 unadvanced after each.  CYCLES 283
! IS MODEL BEHAVIOUR; no documented time exists for a no-op'd level.
!
! INJECTIONS, each alone, saved copy, restored and compared with cmp --
! OBSERVED across all three cwf_ decks:
!   VflInt (prog && v.a.i1 == 0) -> False   -> CYCLES 287, nothing else
!   Connective (prog && c.a.i1 == 0) -> False -> CYCLES 287, nothing else
! (the six DF and AD clause injections, and both execute() AD guard removals, leave it at 283.)
        SLC, (8)300.0
START   LV, $X0, A8                  ! X0's value field := 8.0
        L(BU,64,8), PAT              ! the accumulator PRELOAD
        L(V+I)(BU,64,8), 0($X0)      ! PROGRESSIVE WITH X0: OP, no-op
        BZOP, $                      ! hang if OP did not come on
        K(BU,64,8), PAT
        BZB, $AE, $                  ! hang if the load landed
        KV, $X0, A8
        BZXE, $                      ! hang if X0 was advanced
        L(BU,64,8), PAT
        C0011(V+I)(BU,64), 0($X0)    ! the connective, same refusal
        K(BU,64,8), PAT
        BZB, $AE, $
        KV, $X0, A8
        BZXE, $
        B, PASS
PASS    BEW, $
        CNOP
        SLC, (8)400.0
PAT     DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525212525240
A8      VF, 8.0
        END, START
